<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ikkeri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ikkeri is a village in the Shimoga district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near Sagar. In the 16th and early 17th centuries it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keladi-nayakas">Keladi Nayakas</a>, who served Vijayanagara and then ruled independently, before they moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bednur">Bidanur</a> around 1639. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghoreshwara-temple">Aghoreshwara Temple</a> survives from that period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ikkeri.jpg" alt="Ikkeri" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikhilb239 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ikkeri_temple_04092016.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
